 "approvalMessage": {
  "approvalNumber": 77,
  "billId": {
   "basePrintNo": "A2150",
   "basePrintNoStr": "A2150-2021",
   "printNo": "A2150A",
   "session": 2021,
   "version": "A"
  },
  "chapter": 792,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 77 Chapter 792\n \n      MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 2150-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT in relation to establishing Brendan's law; and to amend the\n        social services law, in relation to  requiring  cordless  window\n        coverings  in  child  day care centers and certain other facili-\n        ties\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This legislation would establish Brendan's Law,  intended  to  protect\nagainst  accidental  injuries  and  deaths associated with corded window\nblinds in certain child care facilities. Specifically, the bill  creates\ndefinitions  to establish the various types of window coverings that may\nbe in use throughout the State, and it amends the Social Services Law to\nrequire that any window blinds newly installed in child care centers  be\ncordless or contain inaccessible operational and inner cords.\n \n  I  fully support the intent of this legislation. We must do everything\nin our power to protect young children from potential danger, and it  is\nof the utmost importance that our youngest New Yorkers are safe in their\nchild  care  settings.  However,  technical changes to the proposed bill\nwere needed to remove certain non-child  care  facilities  that  do  not\nserve  this  vulnerable  young  population,  to  make replacement window\ncovering requirements apply  prospectively,  and  to  require  that  any\npreexisting  window  coverings,  already installed at the time this bill\nbecomes effective are maintained securely and are inaccessible to  chil-\ndren in accordance with regulation. I have reached an agreement with the\nLegislature  to  make  the  necessary  changes and, on the basis of that\nagreement, I am pleased to sign this bill into law.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n\n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2022
 },
